        <p class="lede">
          The best protein powder for hot coffee is collagen peptides, because they dissolve instead of clumping. The best for complete protein is an unflavored whey isolate, tempered in a splash of cool milk before the hot coffee goes in. And the best for iced coffee is a coffee-flavored whey you can shake with milk and ice. Pick by how you drink your coffee, then mix it the right way.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="quick-comparison" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Quick Comparison: The Best Protein Powders for Coffee
          </h2>

          <p>
            The short version: for hot coffee, use collagen peptides, because they dissolve instead of clumping. For a full, complete protein in coffee, use an unflavored whey isolate and mix it the right way, which mostly means tempering it in a little cool liquid or letting the coffee cool slightly first. For iced coffee and shaker-bottle lattes, a coffee-flavored whey is the least effort and tastes the most like a drink you would buy. The table below lines up the seven picks on the numbers that matter, all read from each label at the time of writing.
          </p>

